{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cfbo3YTX2hDnopxNNmc2L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe structure is clean and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- **Right unit, no duplication.** The level computation now has two call sites — `OwnerMapper` (the response field) and `AuditOwnerCreated` (the audit line). Extracting it into a single `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` is exactly the right move: it avoids the inline mapper expression being duplicated into the audit function, and the Javadoc explicitly names itself as the single source of truth. The spec's requirement that the audit record the level is satisfied by reusing that same helper rather than re-deriving.\n\n- **Follows the existing idiom.** `MembershipLevel` mirrors the established `Regions` helper almost exactly: `final` class, private constructor, static derivation method, a named boundary constant (`MAX` ↔ `UNKNOWN`), and thorough field-referencing Javadoc. A maintainer would find it immediately familiar.\n\n- **Package placement is defensible.** `Regions` lives in `mapper` because it is a mapper-only concern; `MembershipLevel` is shared by the mapper and a REST function, so the neutral `model` package (alongside `Owner`, whose fields drive it) is the more natural home.\n\n- **No catch-all growth.** The new class does one thing; `AuditOwnerCreated` and `CountHouseholdMembers` each gained only what the spec required, and `CountHouseholdMembers`'s doc comment was correctly updated to drop the now-obsolete GOLD-tier rationale while honestly noting the count is retained for reporting.\n\n- **OpenAI schema and the removed tier** are consistently retired in favour of `membershipLevel`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_read_input_tokens":24873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":